hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21063","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from a woman called Raja, she said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a woman came to him with a son of hers, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah for me for blessing in him, for three have died for me. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: since you embraced Islam? She said: yes. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: a strong shield. Then a man said to me: listen, O Raja, to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says."
"21064","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, he said: a woman who used to come to us called Mawiyyah narrated to us, she used to be afflicted in her children. And I came to Ubaydullah ibn Mamar al-Qurashi, and with him was a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that man narrated that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of hers, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah, blessed and exalted is He, to keep him for me, for three before him have died for me. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: since you embraced Islam? She said: yes. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: a strong shield. Mawiyyah said: Ubaydullah ibn Mamar said to me: listen, O Mawiyyah. Muhammad said: then she left Ubaydullah ibn Mamar and came to us and narrated to us this hadith."
